From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: aquarat <3090997+aquarat@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] net: atlantic: atl2: keep the station MAC unicast filter
 enabled

Since the AQC113 (ATL2) filter rework in 7.2, the station MAC address is
programmed into the L2 unicast filter at the firmware-reported
l2_filters_base_index, and the unicast/multicast list follows it at
base + 1 .. base + count. hw_atl2_hw_packet_filter_set() still calls
hw_atl_b0_hw_packet_filter_set(), whose loop enables filter i (1..32)
only when i <= mc_list_count. With a non-zero base index, every
packet_filter_set (aq_nic_start, each ndo_set_rx_mode) switches the
station MAC filter off unless base <= mc_list_count. Unicast frames to
the interface's own address then get no UC tag and the L2_PROMISC_OFF
action resolver entry drops them. Broadcast still works (bc_flr_tag),
so DHCP succeeds while unicast traffic is lost; promiscuous mode hides
the problem.

Give ATL2 its own packet_filter_set that does the B0 work but enables
the unicast filters relative to l2_filters_base_index, and bound the
list in hw_atl2_hw_multicast_list_set() against the entries left after
the base index.

On the built-in AQC113 of an M1 Max Mac Studio the firmware reports base
index 9: unicast RX stopped with eight multicast addresses and came back
when a ninth was added.

Tested: 7.2.11 (AsahiLinux asahi-wip), M1 Max Mac Studio, built-in 10GbE:
unicast RX works with promiscuous mode off.
Signed-off-by: aquarat <3090997+aquarat@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 .../aquantia/atlantic/hw_atl2/hw_atl2.c       | 50 ++++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 48 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/net/ethernet/aquantia/atlantic/hw_atl2/hw_atl2.c b/drivers/net/ethernet/aquantia/atlantic/hw_atl2/hw_atl2.c
index 25dd7150a..037848c48 100644
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/aquantia/atlantic/hw_atl2/hw_atl2.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/aquantia/atlantic/hw_atl2/hw_atl2.c
@@ -759,9 +759,55 @@ static int hw_atl2_hw_ring_tx_init(struct aq_hw_s *self,
 static int hw_atl2_hw_packet_filter_set(struct aq_hw_s *self,
 					unsigned int packet_filter)
 {
+	struct aq_nic_cfg_s *cfg = self->aq_nic_cfg;
+	struct hw_atl2_priv *priv = self->priv;
+	u32 base = priv->l2_filters_base_index;
+	u32 vlan_promisc;
+	u32 l2_promisc;
+	unsigned int i;
+
 	hw_atl2_hw_new_rx_filter_promisc(self, IS_FILTER_ENABLED(IFF_PROMISC));
 
-	return hw_atl_b0_hw_packet_filter_set(self, packet_filter);
+	/* Same as hw_atl_b0_hw_packet_filter_set(), except for the L2
+	 * unicast filter enables: on ATL2 the station MAC lives at the
+	 * FW-reported l2_filters_base_index (not at index 0) and the
+	 * UC/MC list follows it.  The B0 loop (indices 1..32, enabled iff
+	 * i <= mc_list_count) would switch the station MAC filter off
+	 * whenever l2_filters_base_index != 0, so unicast frames get no
+	 * UC tag and are dropped by the L2_PROMISC_OFF ART entry.
+	 */
+	l2_promisc = IS_FILTER_ENABLED(IFF_PROMISC) ||
+		     !!(cfg->priv_flags & BIT(AQ_HW_LOOPBACK_DMA_NET));
+	vlan_promisc = l2_promisc || cfg->is_vlan_force_promisc;
+
+	hw_atl_rpfl2promiscuous_mode_en_set(self, l2_promisc);
+
+	hw_atl_rpf_vlan_prom_mode_en_set(self, vlan_promisc);
+
+	hw_atl_rpfl2multicast_flr_en_set(self,
+					 IS_FILTER_ENABLED(IFF_ALLMULTI) &&
+					 IS_FILTER_ENABLED(IFF_MULTICAST), 0);
+
+	hw_atl_rpfl2_accept_all_mc_packets_set(self,
+					      IS_FILTER_ENABLED(IFF_ALLMULTI) &&
+					      IS_FILTER_ENABLED(IFF_MULTICAST));
+
+	hw_atl_rpfl2broadcast_en_set(self, IS_FILTER_ENABLED(IFF_BROADCAST));
+
+	for (i = 0; i < HW_ATL2_MAC_MAX; i++) {
+		u32 en;
+
+		if (i == base)
+			en = 1U;
+		else if (i > base && i <= base + cfg->mc_list_count)
+			en = cfg->is_mc_list_enabled ? 1U : 0U;
+		else
+			en = 0U;
+
+		hw_atl_rpfl2_uc_flr_en_set(self, en, i);
+	}
+
+	return aq_hw_err_from_flags(self);
 }
 
 #undef IS_FILTER_ENABLED
@@ -777,7 +823,7 @@ static int hw_atl2_hw_multicast_list_set(struct aq_hw_s *self,
 	struct aq_nic_cfg_s *cfg = self->aq_nic_cfg;
 	int err = 0;
 
-	if (count > (HW_ATL2_MAC_MAX - HW_ATL2_MAC_MIN)) {
+	if (count > (HW_ATL2_MAC_MAX - base_location)) {
 		err = -EBADRQC;
 		goto err_exit;
 	}
